  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened institutional capacity of workers&apos; organizations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Through this Country Programme Outcome, the ILO will strengthen the capacity of workers&#x2019; organisations in India to engage in effective and evidence-based social dialogue in an economy shaped by rapid technological change, artificial intelligence, evolving trade relations and the implementation of the four Labour Codes.
The CPO will enhance the ability of the 11 Central Trade Unions (CTUs) to respond to structural challenges including informality, wage pressures and uneven enforcement of labour standards. By strengthening macroeconomic literacy and negotiation skills, the Office will enable informed engagement on Labour Codes implementation, the India&#x2013;EU Free Trade Agreement and labour provisions in global value chains.

The ILO will support coordinated action among CTUs and unions representing emerging sectors&#x2014;particularly platform workers&#x2014;through the establishment of a joint working group and strengthened organising strategies. Focus will be placed on youth and women leadership empowerment, improved representation of informal and migrant workers, and coordinated action on occupational safety and health (OSH) and prevention of sexual harassment (POSH). Through these efforts, the CPO will promote inclusive dialogue mechanisms and strengthen workers&#x2019; voice in shaping labour market governance across India&#x2019;s evolving world of work.</narrative>
  </description>
